mour, and piercing insight</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/kay-meek-arts-centre-english-sc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/theatre-la-seizieme-songes-turbulents-comedie-francaise-lumieres-sc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790120522836-HV0E42PKV9Y52QYVVKO7/260503-CF-lumiere051+copy+%281%29.jpg\" alt=\"Lumières, lumières, lumières draws on a Virginia Woolf work at Théâtre la Seizième, October 14 to 18\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>Coproduction by Comédie-Française (Paris) and Les songes turbulents (Montréal) explores the passage of time in post-Victorian England</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/theatre-la-seizieme-songes-turbulents-comedie-francaise-lumieres-sc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/red-demon-firehall-arts-centre-rice-and-beans-theatre\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790825838118-RX11RGAO3588X31RW6SQ/mayumi+yoshida.jpeg\" alt=\"Red Demon speaks three languages at the Firehall Arts Centre\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>Director Mayumi Yoshida takes on challenges of translation in Hideki Noda’s darkly comedic play about people struggling with mistrust as they try to understand one another across linguistic gulfs</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/red-demon-firehall-arts-centre-rice-and-beans-theatre\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/boca-del-lupo-siminovitch-prize-finalists\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790825129941-BPIYG0C6TT83XPGZS1S2/PSP%2B2026%2B-%2BSherry%2B%252B%2BJay%2B-%2BHeadshot%2B_%2BPhoto%2Bportrait.jpg\" alt=\"Boca del Lupo’s Sherry J. Yoon and Jay Dodge make 2026 Siminovitch Prize shortlist\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>B.C. contenders for Canada’s largest theatre prize join finalists from Montreal and Calgary</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/boca-del-lupo-siminovitch-prize-finalists\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/deadly-dinner-party-improv-centre\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790712529313-LE94RSUJN1K6Y3VMQ246/TIC+-+Deadly+Dinner+Party+2026+-+Feat.+Chris+Casillan%2C+Jacki+Gunn%2C+Caitlin+Maira%2C+Meaghan+Hommy%2C+Alan+Pavlakovic-300ppi-PRINT.jpg\" alt=\"Comedy review: Improv Centre’s Deadly Dinner Party serves up killer comedy\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>Audience “assistance” ensures the mystery story’s plot twists always verge on the absurd, right up to the riotous final scene</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/deadly-dinner-party-improv-centre\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/vascular-necrosis-touchstone-glitch\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790694772906-5L1U5PXZWE9W6M5IQD4H/Vascular+Necrosis_Evelyn+Chew--Gabrielle+Nebrida-Pe%CC%81pin--Marguerite+Hanna_photo+credit+Chelsey+Stuyt.jpeg\" alt=\"Jordyn Wood’s lifelong love of writing leads zombie tale Vascular Necrosis to the stage\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>New blend of horror, dark comedy, and queer romance emerges from Touchstone Theatre development program and Glitch Theatre’s disability-led approach</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/vascular-necrosis-touchstone-glitch\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/heist-review-arts-club-theatre\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790537009102-FG4CC6BHAGXJZGGT7BOR/heist-0371-s.jpg\" alt=\"Theatre review: Arts Club’s complex Heist unfolds with seamless efficiency\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>With live visual tricks and countless technical cues, the tale of high-tech burglary builds the momentum needed to pull off Arun Lakra’s time-jumping storyline </p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/heist-review-arts-club-theatre\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/metro-theatre-nuncrackers-sc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1789754031881-P8DMGFPD36AFY50Y1WY5/1.jpg\" alt=\"Nuncrackers brings a zany holiday variety show to Metro Theatre, October 23 to November 14\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>Sequel to the beloved musical comedy <em>Nunsense</em> sets the sisters in a school basement recording a cable-access Christmas special</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/metro-theatre-nuncrackers-sc\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/epidermis-circus-surrey-arts-centre-ws\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">\n        <p><img src=\"https://images.squarespace-cdn.com/content/v1/5f10a7f0e4041a480cbbf0be/1790209252121-50FSJML61MW6INVZCR3A/snafu-epidermis-circus-sexy-puppet-show-ingrid-hansen-photographer-helene-cyr1-puppetry-in-victoria.webp\" alt=\"Puppet show Epidermis Circus gets weird at Surrey Arts Centre on October 2\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" referrerpolicy=\"no-referrer\" />\n\n  \n\n  \n\n    \n\n    \n\n    </p>\n  </a>\n\n    \n    \n\n    \n  \n\n\n          \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n            \n              \n              <p>In the SNAFU Society of Unexpected Spectacles production, <em>Fraggle Rock</em> puppeteer Ingrid Hansen brings a little stinker named Baby Tyler to adorably sassy life</p>\n            \n            \n            \n            <p><a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/epidermis-circus-surrey-arts-centre-ws\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" target=\"_blank\">Read more →</a></p>\n          \n        \n      \n        \n          \n          \n\n\n  \n    \n      <a href=\"https://www.createastir.ca/articles/the-cultch-job\" rel=\"noopener nofollow\" t